# 10. GEMINI AI SHRIMP HEALTH SCANNER

This is one of the most important modules.

Build a multimodal AI-based shrimp health screening system using the Gemini API through the backend.

Allow farmers to upload:
1. Whole shrimp photographs.
2. Gill close-up photographs.
3. Head and hepatopancreas photographs.
4. Muscle photographs.
5. Gut and faeces photographs.
6. Multiple-shrimp photographs.

The AI should examine visible abnormalities such as:
- Colour changes.
- Gill discolouration.
- Visible lesions.
- Muscle opacity.
- Abnormal body appearance.
- Empty or abnormal gut appearance.
- Visible fouling.
- Shell abnormalities.
- Other observable physical changes.

Possible disease and condition knowledge categories include:
- White Spot Syndrome Virus (WSSV).
- Enterocytozoon hepatopenaei (EHP).
- Acute hepatopancreatic necrosis disease (AHPND/EMS).
- Infectious hypodermal and haematopoietic necrosis virus (IHHNV).
- Infectious myonecrosis virus (IMNV).
- Taura syndrome virus (TSV).
- Yellow head virus (YHV).
- White faeces syndrome.
- White muscle conditions.
- Black gill conditions.
- Soft shell problems.
- Red body conditions.
- Other recognised shrimp health conditions.

IMPORTANT MEDICAL AND SCIENTIFIC SAFETY REQUIREMENTS:

A photograph alone cannot reliably confirm most shrimp pathogens.

The scanner must:
- Identify visible observations.
- Provide possible explanations and risk indicators.
- Explain uncertainty.
- Never present an unconfirmed pathogen as a confirmed diagnosis.
- Recommend appropriate laboratory testing where necessary.
- Recommend expert consultation for serious signs.
- Avoid prescribing antibiotics, chemicals or medicines automatically.
- Include an unable-to-identify option.
- Request a clearer photograph when image quality is poor.

Each scan should save:
- Farmer ID.
- Pond ID.
- Culture-cycle ID.
- Image.
- Scan date.
- Visible findings.
- Possible conditions.
- Confidence or uncertainty information.
- Suggested next observations.
- Expert review status.
- Laboratory confirmation status.

Build an expert annotation system so verified labels can eventually support a custom AI training dataset.

